            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is mocking [how 'nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons' does this](https://github.com/nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons/blob/9793801f974bba70e4ac5d7eae6c4f5659993d8e/lua/nvim-web-devicons.lua#L15) (i.e. it [does not include filetypes](https://github.com/nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons/blob/9793801f974bba70e4ac5d7eae6c4f5659993d8e/lua/nvim-web-devicons.lua#L62-L66)).\r\n\r\nIf anything, 'utilyre/barbecue.nvim' needs to use `get_icon` here, which is the intended use in this kind of situations. It was changed [here](https://github.com/utilyre/barbecue.nvim/commit/4c43a3cf31ac10c564f5df30385f57e9c81c0465), yet I am still not sure why. Or add direct support for 'mini.icons'.\r\n\r\nClosing as working as expected.",
